# coder.grid - pixel-art sprite for the record-stitch overlay (openspec
# change record-stitch-overlay, D8). Original art. gen-coder-sprite.py turns
# it into coder-work-01..08.png and coder-idle-01..04.png (192x192 RGBA).
#
# Format:
#   - Lines starting with '#' and blank lines between blocks are ignored.
#   - "palette <char> #rrggbb" declares one opaque colour per character.
#     All palette lines come before the first frame. '.' is reserved for
#     transparent and is never declared.
#   - "frame <work|idle>-NN" starts a frame; exactly 32 rows of exactly 32
#     palette characters follow, with no blank or comment lines inside.
#   - Exactly work-01..work-08 then idle-01..idle-04, in that order.
#
# After editing, regenerate and commit the PNGs:
#   python3 ticket-auto-pipeline/lib/record-assets/gen-coder-sprite.py
# (test-record-assets.sh fails while the PNGs and this file disagree.)

# outline
palette O #0b0d10
# hair
palette H #6b3f22
# hair highlight
palette h #93603a
# skin
palette S #f2c08a
# skin shade
palette s #c98e5c
# eye
palette E #1a1d22
# hoodie
palette C #2fa4a9
# hoodie shade
palette c #1d7478
# sleeve highlight
palette A #6fd3d6
# trousers
palette P #3b4766
# shoes
palette W #d0d4da
# chair
palette R #5a6070
# chair shade
palette r #353a45
# desk top
palette D #d19a5b
# desk front
palette d #9a6534
# desk leg
palette L #6e4523
# monitor frame
palette M #8a93a3
# monitor stand
palette m #4a515e
# screen
palette G #10243a
# screen glow edge
palette g #1d4a6e
# code green
palette 1 #7ee787
# code blue
palette 2 #79c0ff
# code orange
palette 3 #ffa657
# code pink
palette 4 #ff7b9c
# cursor
palette X #f0f6fc
# keyboard
palette K #5c6470
# key
palette k #aab3c0
# mug
palette U #e05d5d

